# The build context for `apps/web/Dockerfile`, and the reason it is not the root
# `.dockerignore`: that file excludes `apps/web/*`, which is exactly what this
# image is made of. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to
# the context root's when one exists, so the two images filter the same tree
# differently without either having to know about the other.
#
# It replaces the root file rather than adding to it, which is why the common
# rules are restated below. Their reasoning is written once, in `.dockerignore`
# at the repository root; only the workspace block at the end is this file's own.

# Version control
.git/

# Installed and built output. The image produces all of it from source, and a
# host copy is stale by definition — worse, it is linked against win32.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
.turbo/
out/
build/
coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Never in an image, in any form.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The workspaces this image does not contain. apps/web's dependency graph
# reaches packages/shared, packages/tokens and packages/api-client and stops
# there — the API and the staff console are neither imported nor served here,
# and apps/api alone is eleven megabytes of migrations and fixtures.
#
# Their manifests are re-included deliberately. A filtered `pnpm install` still
# resolves --frozen-lockfile against every workspace member the lockfile names,
# so a missing package.json fails the install outright; it is the sources that
# are dead weight, not the two files that describe them.
apps/api/*
apps/admin/*
!apps/api/package.json
!apps/admin/package.json

# Test, editor and agent artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documents and planning. Nothing here is read while the site is compiled or
# served.
docs/
plans/
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/*.log.err
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
